This implementation uses nested loops to compare each element of the list with all subsequent elements to check for duplicates. The `are_equal` function is used to compare the elements, considering the specific requirements for string comparison, None values, nested lists, and custom classes.

Note that the time complexity of this implementation is O(n^3) due to the nested loops, where n is the length of the input list. This means that the execution time will increase significantly for larger input lists.

